SUMMARY:Organic Reflections: Celebrating American Composers
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster trumpeter Doug Albert will join organist Larry Hershey in a concert “Celebrating American Composers” at First Reformed Church of Lancaster on Friday\, May 1 at 8 PM.  The free 30 minute concert  will include Aaron Copeland’s “At the RIver”\, Joseph Brackett’s rendition of the Shaker song\, “Simple Gifts”\, and Carmen Dragon’s beloved arrangement of “America\, the Beautiful”. \n\n\n\nThe First Friday “Organic Reflections” concert series is a gift to the community from First Reformed Church\, a center city congregation of the United Church of Christ.  Only 30 minutes in length\, the free concerts begin at 8 PM each First Friday for the convenience of those who wish to spend the early evening visiting downtown galleries before the concert.  Doors open at 7:30 pm.  All are welcome to hear 30 minutes of majestic music that will refresh your soul and inspire your spirit.  
URL:https://visitlancastercity.com/event/organic-reflections-celebrating-american-composers/
LOCATION:First Reformed Church\, 40 E Orange Street\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17602\, United States
CATEGORIES:First Friday,Free Events and Activites,Music and Dance
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/gif:https://visitlancastercity.com/wp-content/uploads/Doug-Albert-Larry-Hershey.gif
ORGANIZER;CN="First Reformed Church":MAILTO:richardweinhold@yahoo.com
END:VEVENT
